Install no shadow when the shadow setting is off

Style::polish() and the tooltip paint now call
ShadowHelper::registerWidget() only when popupShadow is true. The
QtQuick popup path reads the same setting before it installs a shadow.
In GTK 2 the accept function returns false for every window when the
setting is off. That also removes the shadow that every OpenOffice
window gets today.

The Qt gate sits at the call sites and not inside the helper. The
helper holds no reference to Options. A gate there needs a new include,
a new member and a reach up to the parent style. Each call site already
holds the options, and the blur helper of the same function reads them
too.

The gate covers the event filter as well. registerWidget() installs the
filter below its own accept test, so a widget that never registers
never gets one. unregisterWidget() stays open, because it removes a
shadow that an earlier value installed.

An application that sets _KDE_NET_WM_FORCE_SHADOW loses its shadow when
the setting is off. The gate runs before the helper reads that
property. A preference of the user wins over a hint of an application.

The style reads the configuration file once, when the application
starts. A new value therefore reaches the applications that start after
the change. A running application keeps its old value. Nothing in the
tree sweeps the polished widgets for any setting. This change adds no
sweep.

The change sits on the branch work/popup-shadow of the local tree, as
the second commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request
!19 on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

